=== BENCHMARK COMPLETE ===

Interpretation guide:
  - ECS core ops should be < 1μs (nanosecond ideally)
  - Barnes-Hut tree build: O(N log N), check scaling with N
  - Gravity acceleration: dominates tick cost at high N
  - SPH density: check neighbor query scaling
  - Full tick: target 16.6ms for 60 Hz (1000 gas particles)
  - Parallel speedup: compare :tick parallel vs sequential

Bottleneck identification:
  - If tree build >> acceleration: tree overhead is the issue
  - If SPH >> hydro force: neighbor finding is the bottleneck
  - If parallel ≈ sequential: write-set contention or thread starvation
  - If full tick >> sum of parts: serialization/barrier overhead
